+# Integration notes for the team (Member 2 work)
+
+My code is additive: new folders only (`training/`, `member2_dev/`, `loadtest/`, `docs/member2/`). `member2_dev/` is a stand-alone test harness; once the team's Django project (US-14) exists, ignore it and plug `training` into the team project as below.
+
+## 1. Plug into the team's Django project
+
+```python
+# settings.py
+INSTALLED_APPS += ["training"]
+MIDDLEWARE += ["training.middleware.RequestLimitsMiddleware"]   # AFTER AuthenticationMiddleware
+ROOT_URLCONF: add  path("api/", include("training.urls"))
+```
+Then `python manage.py migrate` (creates `TrainingRun`).
+
+## 2. Settings I read (all optional; defaults shown)
+
+| Setting | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `WBMME_ARTIFACT_ROOT` | **required** | Folder for trained models. Must be OUTSIDE any web root (MLE-SR-004) |
+| `WBMME_DATA_ROOT` | placeholder only | Used by the placeholder dataset locator |
+| `WBMME_DATASET_LOCATOR` | `training.locator.default_locator` | **Dotted path to `fn(user_id, dataset_id) -> Path`**, raising `training.locator.DatasetNotFound` when the user does not own it |
+| `WBMME_ROLE_GETTER` | `training.quota.default_role` | **Dotted path to `fn(user) -> "student" / "data_scientist" / "admin"`** |
+| `WBMME_JOB_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | 300 | Training job time limit |
+| `WBMME_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE` | 60 | Requests per user per minute under `/api/` |
+| `WBMME_MAX_REQUEST_BYTES` | 10 MB | Larger bodies get 413 |
+| `WBMME_JOB_ISOLATION` | True | Run training in a separate process (leave on) |
+| `WBMME_JOBS_INLINE` | False | Tests only |
+
+## 3. What I need from other members
+
+- **Vikas (US-01 dataset storage):** write `locate(user_id, dataset_id)` returning the CSV path and set `WBMME_DATASET_LOCATOR`. Until then the placeholder reads `<WBMME_DATA_ROOT>/<user_id>/<dataset_id>.csv`.
+- **Tejas (US-15/17 login and roles):** `request.user` must be a normal Django user. Write the role function above (or give users a group called "Data Scientist" and staff = Admin, which the default already understands). Remove the `/dev/login` routes of `member2_dev`.
+- **Front end:** send the CSRF token in the `X-CSRFToken` header on POST requests, and poll `GET /api/train/<id>` for status.
+
+## 4. What others can use from my code
+
+- `training.catalogue` (models and parameter ranges), `training.params.validate_params`.
+- `training.pipeline.load_split(csv, target, test_size, seed)` rebuilds the exact test split of a run, for evaluation (US-10).
+- `training.artifacts.artifact_path(user_id, run_id)` and `joblib.load(...)` give the fitted pipeline; `TrainingRun` holds model, parameters, target, test size and seed.
+
+## 5. Known limits
+
+- The rate limit and the one-job quota lock work inside one server process. With several processes, use a shared Django cache and a database lock.
+- Admin job quota (2) is my assumption; the SRS table lists only Student and Data Scientist.
+- The default pipeline fills missing values and one-hot encodes text itself; when the data-preparation stories (US-04/05) land, they should pass their choices in instead.
